{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"tt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Terrestrial Time days since noon on January 1, 2000."}]}],"name":"tt"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Terrestrial Time is used for calculations not involving Earth’s rotation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(planetary orbits, eclipses, etc.). This initializer is the inverse of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime\/init(ut:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" — it starts from a TT value and derives the corresponding UT.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If TT falls in a positive discontinuity gap in the selected Delta T model,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"UT clamps to the first representable coordinate after the jump while TT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remains unchanged. At a negative jump with two solutions, fixed-point","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iteration returns the first solution reached from its initial ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ut = tt"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"estimate. Because ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" stores UT, encoding a gap-clamped value and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decoding it derives TT again from the selected model.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nonfinite or nonconvergent input produces an invalid time with NaN fields.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a time from Terrestrial Time days since J2000.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime\/init(tt:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime\/init(tt:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tt"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Initializer","title":"init(tt:)","symbolKind":"init","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:12AstronomyKit9AstroTimeV2ttACSd_tcfc"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime"]]},"references":{"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstroTime":{"title":"AstroTime","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/astrotime","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Represents a moment in time for astronomical calculations."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AstroTime","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AstroTime","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/AstroTime/init(tt:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"tt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a time from Terrestrial Time days since